# Headers of the static pages (Workers static assets, developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/).
# The pages whose scripts ask the Worker for a signed-in reader hold a session's CSRF token: no other
# site may frame them, and they run this site's own files only (no inline script or style: Astro
# writes every script as a file, astro.config.mjs). The account page (Phase 5); /submit/ and a
# paper's page (Phase 6) — `:slug` is one segment, so the Code ↔ Paper reader (/paper/<slug>/code/),
# which reads Europe PMC and Hugging Face, keeps its own rules. The GitHub side (night phase 01):
# the pages that start an authorized action (/new/, /new/link/, /new/import/, /repositories/), the
# callback page of GitHub's authorization (/forge/authorized/: no Referer at all, so the code in
# its address never leaves), and the repository pages (/r/*), which also read GitHub's anonymous API
# and raw files in the reader's browser, on the reader's own quota (D00-5).
/account/
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: same-origin

